{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV2idSSSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"id"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/id","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies an id reference."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/id"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/id":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/id","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/id","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T